            <ArticleTitle>Clinical Inquiries: Can mobile technology improve weight loss in overweight and obese patients?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-113</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Yes, this technology can help in the short term. Mobile technology compared with minimal or no intervention increases short-term (⟨6 months) weight loss (1.4 to 2.7 kg) in overweight and obese patients. Interventions that combine nonelectronic measures with mobile technology increase weight loss more effectively (3.7 kg) than no intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
